  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;denote the fractional part of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and the greatest integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi></math> respectively of a real number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> are three consecutive terms of a G.P. then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to__",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "21",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msubsup><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br />and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are in Geometric progression</p><p>So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>10</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
